  "model": "medium",
  "language": "en",
  "text": "1.6. But even Hollywood itself has become more multinational. In 1991, Hollywood made around 30% of its money from sales of international cinema tickets. However, in 2023, Mission Impossible Dead Reckoning Part 1 made around $235 million in its first five days, but only around 34% of ticket sales came from domestic audiences in the U.S. The remaining 66% came from people watching the movie in different markets worldwide. Around 10% of international sales during this opening week, worth an astonishing $25 million, came from China alone. This is not surprising, given that China accounted for over $136 million worth of sales for a previous Mission Impossible film.",
